TASK 7 (WebDAV source) + TASK 8 (remove Audiobookshelf). This is the largest task. Implement carefully and do NOT run any build/analyze/test (captain does the final verification).

PREREQUISITES already done by the captain:
- `Servers.type` column exists (values: 'navidrome', 'subsonic', 'webdav'; null = legacy Subsonic-compatible). `ServerRepository.addServer/updateServer` accept a `type` param.
- `activeSubsonicClientProvider` returns `null` when `server.type == 'webdav'`.
- `pubspec.yaml` now has `xml: ^7.0.1` (and `dio` already present).
- ARB has NO `audiobooksPodcasts` anymore (you must remove its usages).
- The audio services already read `PlayableItem.headers` (captain wired that). You just need to create `PlayableItem`s with `headers` in the browse screen.

=== NEW FILE 1: `lib/data/webdav/webdav_client.dart` ===
```dart
import 'dart:convert';
import 'package:dio/dio.dart';
import 'package:xml/xml.dart';

class WebDavEntry {
  const WebDavEntry({
    required this.name,
    required this.href,
    required this.isDirectory,
    this.contentType,
  });
  final String name;
  final String href;
  final bool isDirectory;
  final String? contentType;
}

class WebDavClient {
  WebDavClient({
    required this.baseUrl,
    required this.username,
    required this.password,
  }) : dio = Dio(BaseOptions(
          followRedirects: true,
          validateStatus: (s) => s != null && s < 400,
        ));

  final String baseUrl;
  final String username;
  final String password;
  final Dio dio;

  Map<String, String> get _authHeaders => <String, String>{
        'Authorization':
            'Basic ${base64Encode(utf8.encode('$username:$password'))}',
      };

  Future<bool> testConnection() async {
    try {
      final uri = Uri.parse(baseUrl);
      final res = await dio.request(
        uri.toString(),
        options: Options(
          method: 'PROPFIND',
          headers: <String, dynamic>{
            ..._authHeaders,
            'Depth': '0',
            'Content-Type': 'application/xml',
          },
        ),
      );
      return res.statusCode == 200 || res.statusCode == 207;
    } catch (_) {
      return false;
    }
  }

  Future<List<WebDavEntry>> list(String path) async {
    final dir = Uri.parse(baseUrl).resolve(path.isEmpty ? '/' : path);
    final res = await dio.request(
      dir.toString(),
      options: Options(
        method: 'PROPFIND',
        headers: <String, dynamic>{
          ..._authHeaders,
          'Depth': '1',
          'Content-Type': 'application/xml',
        },
      ),
    );
    final body = res.data is String
        ? res.data as String
        : res.data.toString();
    final doc = XmlDocument.parse(body);
    final selfHref = dir.path.endsWith('/') ? dir.path : '${dir.path}/';
    final entries = <WebDavEntry>[];
    for (final resp in doc.findAllElements('response')) {
      final href = resp.findElements('href').firstOrNull?.text.trim() ?? '';
      final rel = href == selfHref
          ? ''
          : Uri.parse(baseUrl).resolve(href).path.replaceFirst(
                Uri.parse(baseUrl).path, '');
      if (rel.isEmpty) continue;
      final collection = resp
          .findAllElements('propstat')
          .expand((e) => e.findElements('prop'))
          .expand((e) => e.findElements('resourcetype'))
          .expand((e) => e.findElements('collection'))
          .isNotEmpty;
      final ct = resp
          .findAllElements('propstat')
          .expand((e) => e.findElements('prop'))
          .expand((e) => e.findElements('getcontenttype'))
          .firstOrNull
          ?.text;
      entries.add(WebDavEntry(
        name: rel.split('/').where((s) => s.isNotEmpty).last,
        href: rel,
        isDirectory: collection,
        contentType: ct,
      ));
    }
    const audioExt = <String>{
      'mp3', 'flac', 'm4a', 'aac', 'ogg', 'opus', 'wav', 'wma', 'dff', 'dsf', 'ape'
    };
    entries.sort((a, b) {
      if (a.isDirectory != b.isDirectory) {
        return a.isDirectory ? -1 : 1;
      }
      return a.name.toLowerCase().compareTo(b.name.toLowerCase());
    });
    return entries
        .where((e) =>
            e.isDirectory ||
            audioExt.contains(e.name.split('.').last.toLowerCase()))
        .toList();
  }
}
```
(Adapt field/element names to the actual `xml` package API — `findAllElements`, `findElements`, `.firstOrNull`, `.text` are correct for `xml: ^7.0.1`.)

=== NEW FILE 2: `lib/data/webdav/webdav_providers.dart` ===
```dart
import 'package:flutter_riverpod/flutter_riverpod.dart';
import '../server_repository.dart';
import 'webdav_client.dart';

final webdavClientProvider = Provider<WebDavClient?>((ref) {
  final server = ref.watch(activeServerProvider);
  if (server == null || server.type != 'webdav') return null;
  return WebDavClient(
    baseUrl: server.baseUrl,
    username: server.username,
    password: server.password,
  );
});

final webdavListingProvider =
    FutureProvider.family<List<WebDavEntry>, String>((ref, path) {
  final client = ref.watch(webdavClientProvider);
  if (client == null) return const <WebDavEntry>[];
  return client.list(path);
});
```

=== NEW FILE 3: `lib/features/webdav/webdav_browse_screen.dart` ===
A `StatefulWidget` (e.g. `WebDavBrowseScreen`) with internal path state starting at `''`. UI:
- A header showing the current path, a back-up button (disabled at root), a folder list, and an audio-file list.
- Tapping a folder sets the path to that folder's `href`. Tapping an audio file plays it: build a queue from ALL audio files in the current directory, start at the tapped index. "Play current directory" plays the whole list from 0.
- Use `ref.watch(webdavClientProvider)` and `ref.watch(webdavListingProvider(path))`.
- For each audio file, build a `PlayableItem`:
  - `id`: the file's relative `href` (stable).
  - `title`: the file name.
  - `streamUrl`: `Uri.parse(client.baseUrl).resolve(file.href).toString()`.
  - `headers`: `{'Authorization': 'Basic ${base64Encode(utf8.encode('${client.username}:${client.password}'))'}`.
  - `albumId`/`artistId`: null.
- Then `ref.read(audioPlayerProvider).setQueue(items, startIndex: index); ...play();`.
- No new route tree — path is internal state only.

